            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the German for to be stuck, then the German for to make an emergency landing."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: stornieren",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "stornieren — \"to cancel (a booking)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Er storniert das Hotel, weil er krank ist. He cancels the hotel because he is ill."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past participle without ge-: ich habe den Flug storniert."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "stornieren was borrowed from Italian stornare 'to turn back, to reverse an entry in the books' (EtymDB), a word from bookkeeping."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
